# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository" button once the repo is public.
#
# TODO BEFORE PUBLISHING (one placeholder left, marked REPLACE):
#   date-released / version — set when you cut the first tag. NOTE: cffconvert
#   validates this file happily with a placeholder date, so it cannot catch a
#   forgotten one. Check it by eye at tag time.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Maestro Career Studio in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Maestro Career Studio: a local-first, evidence-backed job-application copilot"
abstract: >-
  Maestro Career Studio consolidates a candidate's resume history into a structured
  Career Knowledge Base, scores resumes against job descriptions with a
  deterministic, reproducible ATS engine that uses no large language model,
  walks a guided gap-analysis workflow, and renders typeset LaTeX and Typst
  application packages. It runs entirely on the user's own machine and can be
  operated through a web UI, an MCP server, or an in-app chat agent. Resume
  bullets compose verbatim from approved knowledge-base evidence rather than
  being generated at render time.
type: software
authors:
  # Matches the copyright line in NOTICE ("Copyright 2026 Seinun LLC — Ajey
  # Dhayashanker Loganathan"), which is the owner-directed attribution of
  # record. It moved out of LICENSE when that became the verbatim Apache text.
  - given-names: Ajey
    family-names: Loganathan
    name-particle: Dhayashanker
    email: ajey@seinun.com
    affiliation: "Seinun LLC"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/seinun-ai/maestro-career-studio"
url: "https://github.com/seinun-ai/maestro-career-studio"
# REPLACE when you cut v0.1.0.
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-01-01"
keywords:
  - resume
  - job-application
  - applicant-tracking-system
  - ats
  - career
  - large-language-models
  - model-context-protocol
  - local-first
  - self-hosted
  - latex
  - typst
